WEBVTT

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:09.032
When you submit Spark S Q L, Spark does not simply read the statement from top to bottom and execute each word

00:00:09.032 --> 00:00:13.422
immediately. It first understands the query and builds a logical plan.

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:18.562
Then it optimizes that plan and produces a physical execution plan.

00:00:18.562 --> 00:00:27.087
The physical plan may include table or file scans, filters, joins, aggregations, sorting, and data exchanges.

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:32.812
An exchange is often a clue that data needs to move between workers.

00:00:32.812 --> 00:00:37.652
You do not need to memorize the entire optimizer.

00:00:37.652 --> 00:00:44.112
The useful habit is to remember that your S Q L is translated into an execution plan,

00:00:44.112 --> 00:00:49.586
and that plan helps explain why one query may be much more expensive than another.
